00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:14.280
Then you look at New Hampshire and you have
Bernie Sanders, um, in first with Pete booted

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:19.540
judge just behind him and Bernie and Biden
rather further down in third place.

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:21.790
So what's the trajectory here?

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:24.349
What is next in 2020?

00:02:24.349 --> 00:02:28.030
The next debate is on January 14th.

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:31.849
So far there are only five candidates who
have qualified.

00:02:31.849 --> 00:02:38.620
Those are Joe Biden, uh, Bernie Sanders, Elizabeth
Warren, Pete judge and Amy Klobuchar.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:44.900
Then, and this is really important, we've
been wondering, is the DNC going to change

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:48.769
the rules to let Mike Michael Bloomberg into
the debates?

00:02:48.769 --> 00:02:53.480
Michael Bloomberg is a billionaire who has
been self funding his campaign and not taking

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.499
individual contributions.

00:02:55.499 --> 00:03:01.069
He very quickly was able to, with the expenditure
of more than a hundred million dollars in

00:03:01.069 --> 00:03:08.310
advertising, get himself five, maybe six,
maybe even 7% in one recent poll, which is

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:12.010
quite remarkable given how short of a time
it's been and it shows that at least to some

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:16.159
degree if you've got some name recognition,
you can buy your way in if you spend enough

00:03:16.159 --> 00:03:18.049
money into a primary.

00:03:18.049 --> 00:03:23.189
We wondered because Bloomberg is not accepting
donations and to get into the debates you

00:03:23.189 --> 00:03:25.469
need to meet certain donor thresholds.

00:03:25.469 --> 00:03:32.200
Would the DNC consider changing the rules
in order to allow Michael Bloomberg into debates?

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:39.140
Uh, starting with the eighth debate in February,
Tom Perez, the DNC chair says that they are

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:45.870
looking at a different system for determining
who will be allowed into the debates.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:52.700
The idea that he's using for cover is, listen,
we have had a system in place before anybody

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:53.890
voted.

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:59.069
Once people start voting, maybe we should
have a different system for determining who

00:03:59.069 --> 00:04:01.090
does or doesn't get into the debates.

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:05.719
Now I've been saying for weeks now they may
do this and this is how they figured out a

00:04:05.719 --> 00:04:08.379
way to maybe have some cover in doing it.

00:04:08.379 --> 00:04:12.810
Our friend Dave Weigel recently interviewed
Tom Perez and here's how the conversation

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:14.050
went.

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:19.340
Um, Dave Weigel asked Mike Bloomberg said
he's not going to raise donor money if he

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:22.830
runs, he's going to sell fund his campaign,
which would prevent him from accessing the

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:24.170
stage under the DNCs rules.

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:28.360
Is there any chance that the DNC relaxes the
donor requirement?

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:33.680
If there's someone in the race who's polling
well or winning States but not raising money,

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:37.200
and Tom Perez said, we have our rules in place
for November and December.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.770
Those rules of both the grassroots fundraising
threshold and upholding threshold that used

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:41.770
to be either or.

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:46.140
As you know Dave, and now it's and for November
and December, those are the rules.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:50.260
We haven't set the rules for after the first
of the new year and that's something that

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:51.360
we're doing right now.

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:55.330
We always set the rules early enough so that
we can give notice to the campaigns.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:57.250
And Dave Weigel said so it's possible.

00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:58.870
It wouldn't be both.

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:00.700
It wouldn't be an and anymore.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:05.650
Meaning both fundraising and polling and Tom
Perez said, we haven't figured it out.

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:10.120
One thing we will consider is what should
the rules of engagement be after people have

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:14.220
started voting, because right now zero votes
have been cast, the voters haven't spoken.

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:19.900
What should the rules be once the voters have
spoken and we have some actual data from States?

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:25.910
That's the question we're considering right
now, so we now have with debate number eight

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:30.350
in February with the requirements needing
to be met in January.

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:37.520
The opportunity for the DNC to change how
they determine who gets into the debates.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:42.800
We're going to keep talking about that because
that could be a big deal in terms of, again,

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:50.740
making the scenario one that ultimately leads
to an establishment centrist being the nominee

00:05:50.740 --> 00:06:48.550
and we'll talk about

00:06:48.550 --> 00:07:24.500
that more in the new year.

